winewayland: use the restored size when a configure ends the maximized state without one

A compositor may answer a window that starts maximized with a configure that
carries neither the maximized state nor a size: the size is left to the
client. Hyprland does so when it cannot predict a tile for the new window:
the window it would split is floating. That was observed with a floating
dialog holding the focus, and with the first window of a workspace while
the focus is elsewhere (DwindleAlgorithm.cpp). The driver then cleared
WS_MAXIMIZE and kept the window at the rectangle it had while maximized.
That rectangle still covers the monitor, so win32u reports the window as
fullscreen and not resizable, the driver announces it with equal minimum and
maximum sizes, and Hyprland maps a window with a fixed size floating. Power
BI Desktop, which starts maximized, came up as a floating window slightly
larger than the monitor instead of a tile.
When a configure ends the maximized state and gives no size, give the window
the size of its restored placement, as restoring it does. It is then an
ordinary resizable window: the compositor tiles it and sends the size of the
tile. Compositors that send no size when a window that started maximized is
restored are served by the same change.
Not for a configure the compositor sent before it saw the window's own
request to be maximized: the answer to that request follows and would
resize the window straight back. The driver sends a wl_display.sync just
before xdg_toplevel.set_maximized, on the event thread's queue, so its
answer is handled in order with the configures; each configure records
whether the sync was still unanswered when it arrived. A reader prepared on
an empty queue holds off every socket read while the listener is set, as
libwayland drops an event that has none. The initial configure is restored
even then: the compositor maps the window from it, and with the maximized
rectangle Hyprland floated the window in 4 of 10 starts (12 of 12 tiled
with this exception).
Applies after wine-11.18-wayland-fixed-dialog-maximized.patch and
wine-11.18-wayland-keep-toplevel-state.patch; without the latter a configure
sequence without a toplevel event would be read as such a request. Wine
master had the same code on 2026-11-18.
Wine-derived change: LGPL-2.1-or-later.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
